# Inventory Item
# Example Business Knowledge expressed in Menata Language
# Domain: Warehouse — items stocked in multiple units of measure
# Case 5 of the Case Portfolio (runtime/case-portfolio.md)
# External benchmark: runtime/benchmarks/006-inventory-warehouse-benchmark.md
# References: inventory-item-unit-conversion.menata
#
# Tier 1 of the Quantity/UoM framework (Study 15): Rice — Base Unit KG, one fixed
# alternate unit (SAK) — needs no Item Unit Conversion record at all, see Stock
# Movement. Tier 2: Cement — Base Unit PCS, multiple alternate units (BOX, DOZEN) —
# needs Item Unit Conversion records (see inventory-item-unit-conversion.menata, a
# separate Object that references back to this one — the ordinary Object References
# pattern, 001-object.md §Relationships; no child-table grammar needed here).

Item

Fields

- Name : Text
- Base Unit : PCS | KG | BOX | SAK
- Minimum Stock Level : Number
- Stock On Hand : Number

Constraints

- Name is required.
- Base Unit is required.

Permissions

Warehouse Staff

- View

Views

- Item Form : Form
- Item List : List
- Low Stock Items : List
- Item Detail : Detail
